#: templates/carbon/methodology.html:8
msgid "Calculation Methodology"
msgstr ""

#: templates/carbon/methodology.html:9
msgid ""
"How every number in this module is produced — in plain language, so "
"anyone on the team can explain a figure without needing a carbon-"
"accounting background."
msgstr ""

#: templates/carbon/methodology.html:15
msgid "The core formula"
msgstr ""

#: templates/carbon/methodology.html:16
msgid ""
"Every activity entry (a litre of diesel, a kWh of electricity, a flight) "
"is converted to carbon dioxide equivalent (CO2e) using one formula, "
"applied consistently everywhere in this module:"
msgstr ""

#: templates/carbon/methodology.html:17
msgid "tCO2e = (Activity Quantity × Emission Factor) ÷ 1000"
msgstr ""

#: templates/carbon/methodology.html:18
msgid ""
"The emission factor converts a physical quantity (litres, kWh, km, kg) "
"into kilograms of CO2-equivalent. Dividing by 1000 converts kilograms to "
"tonnes, the standard unit for corporate GHG reporting."
msgstr ""

#: templates/carbon/methodology.html:22
msgid "The three Scopes (GHG Protocol)"
msgstr ""

#: templates/carbon/methodology.html:24
msgid "SCOPE 1"
msgstr ""

#: templates/carbon/methodology.html:24
msgid ""
"Direct emissions from sources the company owns or controls — company "
"vehicles, on-site generators, refrigerant leaks."
msgstr ""

#: templates/carbon/methodology.html:25
msgid "SCOPE 2"
msgstr ""

#: templates/carbon/methodology.html:25
msgid ""
"Indirect emissions from purchased electricity, heat, steam or cooling. "
"Reported two ways: location-based (grid average) and market-based (your "
"actual electricity contracts, e.g. a renewable PPA)."
msgstr ""

#: templates/carbon/methodology.html:26
msgid "SCOPE 3"
msgstr ""

#: templates/carbon/methodology.html:26
msgid ""
"Everything else in the value chain — business travel, employee commuting,"
" purchased goods, waste, and 12 other categories defined by the GHG "
"Protocol Scope 3 Standard."
msgstr ""

#: templates/carbon/methodology.html:31
msgid "Year-on-year comparison"
msgstr ""

#: templates/carbon/methodology.html:32
msgid ""
"YoY change is only ever calculated against a prior period's closed, "
"stored total — never a live recalculation of an open period. This avoids "
"a moving-target comparison, which was one of the errors found in the "
"earlier consultant-built spreadsheets this module replaces."
msgstr ""

